  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The function \n$f(x,y)$\nhas the first derivative\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} & y{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(0,0).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(0,0)<0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(0,0)$ is a local minimum of $f$",
